<h1>Legio VI Victrix in History</h1>

<p> The name "Legio VI", the Sixth Legion, can refer to two separate
  legions.  The first was raised by Gaius Julius Caesar in Gaul in 52
  BC and fought in the Gallic Wars, the Caesarian Civil War, and then
  later in Judea and Syria.  In about 48 BC, it earned the title
  <em>Ferrata</em> ("Ironsides").  A second Legio VI, a largely if not
  entirely different set of troops, was raised in 41 BC by Octavian.
  The two sixth legions fought on different sides in the Battle of
  Actium, which saw Antony (and Legio VI Ferrata) defeated.  VI
  Ferrata's remaining troops moved to Judea and Syria, while
  Octavian's Legio VI returned to Hispania.  Some time before 60 AD,
  Octavian's Legio VI in Hispania was awarded the title
  <em>Victrix</em>, and it is this legion that we reenact.


